invariant: INV-17
file: src/chacha20_avx512.c
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: chacha20_avx512_xor returns without calling avx512_wipe_registers,
  so the key words, the state and the keystream it ran through the 512-bit
  registers stay there after the call. Every byte it writes is still
  right, so no vector sees it. The script compiles the kernel for x86-64
  and requires the call in chacha20_avx512_xor.

--- old
    // registers, and the compiler clears none of them on return.
    chacha_lanes_wipe_registers();
--- new
    // registers, and the compiler clears none of them on return.
